WEBVTT

00:23.331 --> 00:24.871
In the 11th century,

00:24.961 --> 00:28.211
the invasion by Denmark's army
and the Vikings

00:28.291 --> 00:30.421
continued to intensify.

00:34.261 --> 00:36.261
ENGLAND 1012 AD

00:44.391 --> 00:46.311
In October,

00:46.401 --> 00:49.821
the attacks, which had continued for several years,

00:49.901 --> 00:51.691
reached a turning point.

00:51.781 --> 00:54.321
VICINITY OF JELLING DENMARK
KING SWEYN'S ESTATE

00:55.151 --> 00:58.821
Are you telling me
to withdraw my troops from England?

00:59.701 --> 01:02.661
We're not withdrawing. We're letting them rest.

01:03.701 --> 01:06.921
Marching in the winter weakens them.

01:08.831 --> 01:12.631
Let the soldiers rest.

01:12.711 --> 01:15.341
Yes, sir. As you wish.

01:16.431 --> 01:17.721
The summer.

01:19.391 --> 01:23.521
We're going to strike next summer.

01:23.601 --> 01:27.441
I, too, shall lead an army in battle.

01:32.271 --> 01:33.651
So, suddenly we get a break?

01:33.731 --> 01:34.991
ENGLAND COAST
DANISH ARMY BASE

01:35.071 --> 01:37.111
I want to go home.

01:37.201 --> 01:40.661
We don't need those pirates for now, either.

01:44.751 --> 01:47.331
I thought I'd be able to earn a lot this year.

01:47.961 --> 01:50.671
We can't do anything,
now that the army is staying put.

01:50.751 --> 01:54.091
This is why I hate being a hired hand.

01:56.421 --> 01:59.341
What's Askeladd going to do?

02:01.971 --> 02:03.511
Askeladd.

02:03.601 --> 02:06.931
It'd be a shame to spend all winter like this.

02:07.021 --> 02:09.851
And we already raided all the good villages.

02:11.061 --> 02:12.481
True.

02:12.571 --> 02:14.481
What are you going to do?

02:14.571 --> 02:16.361
We can't do anything about it.

02:18.321 --> 02:20.491
We're going to do what the birds do.

02:20.571 --> 02:23.871
We'll go to where the food is.

02:39.051 --> 02:41.971
KINGDOM OF FRANCE
VICINITY OF LOIRE RIVER

02:42.721 --> 02:44.471
Don't just stand there.

02:49.521 --> 02:50.771
They have a ram.

02:50.851 --> 02:52.481
Bring the crossbowmen.

02:52.561 --> 02:55.731
One. Two.

02:57.861 --> 02:59.451
Alternate fire with two groups.

02:59.531 --> 03:00.861
Aim.

03:02.031 --> 03:02.951
Fire.

03:10.581 --> 03:12.501
It's no good. Retreat.

03:33.231 --> 03:35.861
It looks like the Franks are fighting
amongst themselves.

03:36.651 --> 03:38.321
The fort's defended by only a few men.

03:38.401 --> 03:41.241
The attackers have 800.

03:41.321 --> 03:44.111
I can't believe they attacked the fort head-on.

03:45.161 --> 03:47.741
So, this is the local clan's headquarters.

03:47.831 --> 03:51.751
How about it? Doesn't it smell like treasure?

03:53.121 --> 03:55.171
So, that's what you're after.

03:55.251 --> 03:56.881
Let's do it, Askeladd.

03:57.921 --> 03:59.251
We'll side with the attackers.

03:59.341 --> 04:04.261
Let's smash open the treasure chest,
and take everything inside.

04:04.341 --> 04:05.761
All right.

04:05.841 --> 04:09.011
I was wondering why we came to the boonies.

04:09.101 --> 04:10.641
You're amazing, Askeladd.

04:10.721 --> 04:13.391
Your predictions were spot-on.

04:13.481 --> 04:15.601
Let's make up our loss from England.

04:15.691 --> 04:17.361
Okay, Thorfinn.

04:17.441 --> 04:19.401
You're up.

04:38.041 --> 04:39.421
We're going to war.

06:15.181 --> 06:16.731
NORMANNI

06:17.271 --> 06:18.391
We're going to war.

06:19.691 --> 06:22.651
Make contact with their leader.

06:22.731 --> 06:24.231
Give him this message:

06:25.151 --> 06:27.441
"You're terrible at battle.

06:27.531 --> 06:28.951
I can't stand watching you.

06:29.031 --> 06:31.621
Therefore, my men will help you.

06:31.991 --> 06:34.201
This is a once-in-a-lifetime offer.

06:34.281 --> 06:38.121
I shall lead you to victory, no matter what.

06:38.711 --> 06:43.461
Once the fort falls, we will take half of the spoils.

06:43.541 --> 06:46.131
We shall attack again tomorrow morning."

06:46.841 --> 06:51.011
After you deliver the message, stay in their camp,
and observe the situation.

06:51.091 --> 06:52.301
Got it? Then go.

06:55.431 --> 06:56.391
What's wrong?

06:57.181 --> 06:58.771
Go, Thorfinn.

07:01.021 --> 07:03.941
Do you have any idea how many people I've killed?

07:11.991 --> 07:13.531
I went scouting,

07:13.621 --> 07:15.451
and I also brought up the rear.

07:18.791 --> 07:21.121
I've accomplished enough.

07:21.211 --> 07:23.581
But you...

07:24.291 --> 07:27.251
What? You want a reward?

07:27.341 --> 07:30.801
If you close the deal, I'll give you three gold pieces.

07:30.881 --> 07:32.931
I swear in the name of Tyr.

07:34.391 --> 07:35.551
Don't test me.

07:36.261 --> 07:38.891
How long do you plan to keep running away?

07:38.971 --> 07:40.931
I'm so scared.

07:41.021 --> 07:43.481
I was just joking.

07:44.521 --> 07:45.771
But you know...

07:46.821 --> 07:51.821
You'd have to bring me at least one head with a helmet,
if you want that.

07:59.581 --> 08:01.121
He never changes.

08:01.791 --> 08:05.131
Are you sure it's okay
to let him handle the negotiation?

08:05.831 --> 08:08.091
Soldiers are short-tempered
when they're weak.

08:08.171 --> 08:11.761
They might kill the messenger,
before the negotiations start. It happens all the time.

08:13.051 --> 08:15.181
Who cares if we lose some kid that follows us?

08:23.021 --> 08:24.851
What are you doing, kid?

08:25.441 --> 08:27.981
This is no place for a kid.

08:28.651 --> 08:30.151
I'm a messenger.

08:30.231 --> 08:32.191
Is there anyone who can speak Norse?

08:32.651 --> 08:35.701
What's wrong with you? What language is that?

08:35.781 --> 08:37.451
He's not a Frank.

08:39.031 --> 08:41.291
Is he a spy from the fort?

08:41.371 --> 08:43.121
Secure him.

08:49.001 --> 08:50.211
I'm a messenger.

08:50.801 --> 08:52.971
Is there anyone who can speak Norse?

08:57.341 --> 09:00.601
You want half of the spoils?

09:01.391 --> 09:04.481
You mercenaries. Don't push your luck.

09:05.561 --> 09:07.941
"You want half of the spoils?
Don't push your luck."

09:08.021 --> 09:10.571
You're pretty confident in yourself.

09:10.651 --> 09:12.861
Normanni kid.

09:13.991 --> 09:15.361
Normanni?

09:15.451 --> 09:17.741
Those people from the north attacking England?

09:17.821 --> 09:19.871
"Those people from the north attacking England?"

09:21.081 --> 09:22.621
Even a kid can see it.

09:23.291 --> 09:26.291
If you keep attacking the front gate,
your men are just going to die.

09:26.371 --> 09:28.381
Their defenses are weak on the lake.

09:28.461 --> 09:31.041
We're going to attack there.

09:31.131 --> 09:32.381
Your plan is ill-considered.

09:32.961 --> 09:36.881
The river that leads to the lake gets steeper upstream.

09:36.971 --> 09:39.141
There's even a waterfall.

09:39.221 --> 09:41.931
Our ship sunk downstream.

09:43.061 --> 09:45.891
That's what would happen
if you attacked from the lake.

09:45.981 --> 09:48.561
"That's what would happen
if you attacked from the lake."

09:48.651 --> 09:51.521
Then do you want to turn down my offer?

09:51.611 --> 09:56.151
Then Askeladd and his hundred men are going
to join the defenders in the fort.

09:57.241 --> 09:58.951
He'll do the same thing if I die too.

09:59.991 --> 10:02.161
If I don't signal that the deal has been closed,

10:02.741 --> 10:05.911
you're going to make enemies
of a hundred fierce men from the Northern Sea.

10:11.541 --> 10:12.461
Very well.

10:12.541 --> 10:13.461
Your Highness.

10:13.551 --> 10:14.591
But...

10:14.671 --> 10:18.301
if you're lying, I'm going to cut off your head.

10:18.881 --> 10:21.971
If you're telling the truth,
then in the name of Jesus Christ,

10:22.051 --> 10:23.431
I'll share my bread equally.

10:23.511 --> 10:25.311
"I'll share my bread equally."

10:26.731 --> 10:29.191
Give me back my dagger.

10:29.271 --> 10:31.061
It's a memento from my father.

10:49.461 --> 10:51.381
It's Thorfinn's signal.

10:51.461 --> 10:53.791
One high arrow, and two low arrows.

10:54.381 --> 10:56.051
Let's hurry.

10:56.131 --> 10:59.301
Let's cross the pass before the moon rises.

11:01.891 --> 11:04.681
We're stuck guarding the ship the whole time.

11:04.761 --> 11:07.061
I want to fight too.

11:07.141 --> 11:09.521
Damn that fat general.

11:12.851 --> 11:13.861
Over there.

11:20.281 --> 11:23.281
It's a dragon!

11:23.371 --> 11:24.831
It's on the mountain.

11:34.081 --> 11:35.751
A dragon?

11:40.011 --> 11:42.511
You said, the dragon climbed the mountain?

11:42.591 --> 11:47.011
Yes. Last night,
the soldiers guarding the ship all reported they saw it.

11:47.471 --> 11:48.721
I see.

11:48.811 --> 11:50.181
It's a bad omen, Your Highness.

11:52.441 --> 11:55.191
I want to see it too.

11:56.231 --> 11:57.151
Kid.

11:57.821 --> 12:00.281
Your friends haven't come yet.

12:00.361 --> 12:01.741
"I want to see it too."

12:01.821 --> 12:04.161
The sun is already up.

12:04.241 --> 12:05.661
"The sun is already up."

12:05.741 --> 12:07.951
Just attack, you fat-ass.

12:08.031 --> 12:09.161
You'll understand soon.

12:10.161 --> 12:13.211
You said something mean just now, didn't you?

12:13.291 --> 12:17.421
It looks like our entertainment for tonight is going
to be cutting off your head.

12:22.011 --> 12:23.881
Forward march.

12:23.971 --> 12:25.891
Forward march.

12:32.351 --> 12:34.351
Forward.

12:38.021 --> 12:39.651
Attack.

12:49.741 --> 12:51.661
Oh, no. It's started.

12:51.751 --> 12:54.161
We're late. Bastards.

12:54.251 --> 12:56.331
Put your heart into it.

12:56.421 --> 12:58.171
The battlefield is waiting.

13:04.261 --> 13:06.051
It'll be the same every time.

13:06.131 --> 13:07.971
Come on.

13:08.051 --> 13:10.061
Put a bridge on the west side too.

13:10.561 --> 13:12.561
I don't care how many men we lose.

13:15.481 --> 13:18.021
Hey. Which one is their leader?

13:19.271 --> 13:21.861
The one with the feather on his helmet.

13:21.941 --> 13:22.821
It's him.

13:25.071 --> 13:26.321
A head with a helmet.

13:31.031 --> 13:32.371
You bastard.

13:32.451 --> 13:34.871
He was lying. Kill him.

13:34.961 --> 13:36.871
Kill the kid.

13:41.341 --> 13:44.301
You bastard.

13:44.381 --> 13:46.681
You let the kid escape.
You haven't captured the fort.

13:46.761 --> 13:49.141
What's wrong with you guys?

13:49.221 --> 13:51.601
You're thinking you'll go home,
once the snow falls.

13:51.681 --> 13:52.851
That's not going to happen.

13:52.931 --> 13:55.141
You're not going home until the fort is captured.

14:09.821 --> 14:10.661
What?

14:55.041 --> 14:58.041
Heave-ho.

15:03.291 --> 15:06.211
Row. Full speed ahead.

15:11.801 --> 15:14.431
Whoever gets there first gets twice as much.

15:14.511 --> 15:15.971
Put your heart into it.

15:18.101 --> 15:19.231
I see.

15:19.311 --> 15:23.731
Those were friendly forces.
All troops, forward. Don't stop until the fort falls.

15:26.191 --> 15:28.491
Never imagined they'd carry their ship over the pass.

15:30.071 --> 15:31.701
Don't hesitate.

15:31.781 --> 15:34.071
Eighty men from the right wing,
go to the boat landing.

15:34.661 --> 15:36.241
Crossbowmen, this way.

15:47.551 --> 15:49.051
Is that all you got?

15:49.551 --> 15:51.591
The lake's not a barrier.

15:51.681 --> 15:54.051
It's a shallow pond that makes for a perfect attack.

15:54.591 --> 15:56.551
Great. We're going in.

16:05.401 --> 16:08.651
What? They pierced my shield,
even though they're so far away.

16:08.731 --> 16:10.821
They got Olov.

16:11.241 --> 16:12.361
Askeladd.

16:12.451 --> 16:13.861
Crossbowmen?

16:13.951 --> 16:16.321
We're going to take a few losses.

16:16.411 --> 16:18.331
This is the perfect chance.

16:18.991 --> 16:21.081
Fire as much as you can before they land.

16:29.711 --> 16:30.711
A child?

16:35.051 --> 16:36.051
What?

16:36.511 --> 16:37.891
They stopped attacking?

16:39.561 --> 16:41.311
Maybe they ran out of arrows.

16:43.601 --> 16:46.061
Men. Prepare to land.

16:46.151 --> 16:47.691
This is our chance.

17:28.271 --> 17:29.861
-Oh, no.
-Kill him.

17:29.941 --> 17:31.441
-This is for the captain.
-Damn.

17:31.521 --> 17:34.151
-That kid's crazy.
-Get him.

17:42.161 --> 17:44.621
Go. Storm them.

17:54.091 --> 17:56.381
All right. Go on a rampage.

18:01.511 --> 18:04.181
Holding the gate's too hard for these guys.

18:05.231 --> 18:07.521
Hurry up, and kill them all, guys.

18:12.231 --> 18:14.281
One. Two.

18:40.341 --> 18:44.141
Those Normannis are crazy.

18:52.151 --> 18:57.151
That fortress was no match
against my military tactics.

18:58.531 --> 19:01.411
The captain of the fortress defense died in battle.

19:01.491 --> 19:05.081
The soldiers said, a kid did it.

19:05.161 --> 19:07.371
That kid?

19:07.451 --> 19:09.871
Never underestimate a Normanni.

19:09.961 --> 19:13.331
If I send him back now,
he's going to become an enemy.

19:13.421 --> 19:15.041
What shall we do?

19:16.301 --> 19:18.721
Those guys came over the pass, right?

19:18.801 --> 19:21.221
They'll probably go back the same way,
carrying the ship.

19:21.301 --> 19:23.141
That's when we'll attack.

19:23.221 --> 19:27.271
A sailor on land is like a baby.

19:30.851 --> 19:32.151
Your Highness.

19:33.441 --> 19:36.071
I have a message for General Jabbathe.

19:36.731 --> 19:39.281
What is it? Tell me.

19:39.361 --> 19:41.321
The treasure room...

19:49.911 --> 19:52.711
Where's my treasure?

19:52.791 --> 19:55.841
They also plundered the church
and the houses of all the leaders.

19:55.921 --> 19:57.921
They took everything.

19:58.001 --> 20:00.421
What?

20:00.511 --> 20:01.801
I see.

20:01.881 --> 20:04.721
I have a message for the leader of the Franks.

20:04.801 --> 20:05.971
What?

20:11.481 --> 20:13.731
As for your half of the spoils,

20:13.811 --> 20:15.901
you get victory,

20:15.981 --> 20:18.271
and we get the treasure.

20:18.361 --> 20:20.231
You're fine with that, right?

20:20.321 --> 20:23.361
I think we're being quite generous here, you know.

20:23.451 --> 20:25.911
We let you have the fort, after all.

20:28.331 --> 20:31.371
-You bastards.
-Oh, no.

20:31.451 --> 20:33.251
-They'll descend the waterfall.
-Savages.

20:33.331 --> 20:35.171
-Get the boats.
-You pirates.

20:35.251 --> 20:38.501
-All boats in the fort have been destroyed.
-You greedy beasts.

20:38.591 --> 20:40.511
You scammers.

20:40.591 --> 20:42.301
You country bumpkins.

20:42.381 --> 20:44.591
I can't understand French.

20:45.641 --> 20:48.221
Now then, shall we call it a night?

20:48.301 --> 20:50.061
Thorfinn hasn't returned.

20:50.141 --> 20:51.811
Oh, really?

20:51.891 --> 20:54.061
Oh, well. I bet he's dead anyway.

20:54.141 --> 20:56.481
Now there's more treasure for us.

21:06.491 --> 21:07.741
You're alive?

21:07.821 --> 21:10.241
You're tough, kid. Did you get hurt?

21:10.331 --> 21:11.161
Askeladd.

21:11.951 --> 21:13.911
It's the captain's head.

21:14.001 --> 21:16.421
Well, did you cut it off?

21:21.301 --> 21:22.961
You promised.

21:23.051 --> 21:24.421
I won't let you say no.

21:28.181 --> 21:31.891
I, warrior from Iceland, son of Thors, Thorfinn,

21:31.971 --> 21:35.981
in the name of my father's sword,
challenge you, Askeladd, to a duel.

21:37.021 --> 21:39.561
To avenge my father's death.

21:39.651 --> 21:41.731
-Hey.
-He wants to duel now?

21:41.821 --> 21:43.941
He's got guts.

21:44.031 --> 21:46.361
I, son of Olaf, Askeladd,

21:46.451 --> 21:49.161
in the name of Artorius, my ancestor,

21:49.241 --> 21:51.411
accept your challenge, Thorfinn.

21:54.001 --> 21:54.831
However...

21:56.001 --> 21:57.421
ask me again later.

21:58.081 --> 21:59.961
We're getting out of here now.

22:00.041 --> 22:01.921
Row, men.

22:02.001 --> 22:06.421
If you don't hurry up, they'll capture the river.

22:06.511 --> 22:09.721
You bastard. Don't play the fool with me.

22:14.311 --> 22:16.101
Who cares if there's a dragon?

22:16.181 --> 22:17.271
I'm not scared.

22:17.351 --> 22:18.391
Right, right.

22:18.481 --> 22:19.691
But you know...

22:25.191 --> 22:26.441
It's here!

22:40.211 --> 22:41.961
Goodbye.

22:42.501 --> 22:45.001
Franks.

22:46.051 --> 22:49.931
-Let's go home.
-We struck it big.

22:50.011 --> 22:51.971
We'll survive the winter.

22:55.061 --> 22:56.601
Yeah.
